# Cafe Billing System

A simple command-line billing program for a small cafe, written in Python. You pick items from a menu, add or remove them from a cart, and get a bill with GST at the end.

## Overview

I made this as my first-year project to practice basic Python. The program shows a menu of 10 items, lets the user build an order, and prints a final bill with subtotal, 5% GST and total. Everything runs in the terminal and needs no extra libraries.

## Features

- Menu with 10 items and their prices (in ₹)
- Add items by typing the name (not case sensitive)
- Remove items or reduce their quantity
- View the cart or menu at any time
- Input checking for quantity (no letters, zero or negative numbers)
- Final bill with subtotal, 5% GST and total
- Won't generate a bill if the cart is empty

## Technologies Used

- Python 3
- Concepts used: dictionaries, functions, `while` loop, `for` loop, `if/elif/else`, `break`, string methods (`strip`, `title`, `isdigit`)

## How to Run

1. Install Python 3 from python.org if you don't have it.
2. Download or clone this repository:
   ```
   git clone <your-repo-link>
   cd <repo-folder>
   ```
3. Run the program:
   ```
   python main.py
   ```
   (Replace `main.py` with your file name.)

## How to Use

| Command | What it does |
|---|---|
| Item name (e.g. `Pizza`) | Adds the item, then asks for quantity |
| `remove` | Removes an item or reduces its quantity |
| `cart` | Shows what is in your cart |
| `menu` | Shows the menu again |
| `done` | Prints the bill and exits |

## Testing

I tested it by hand with these cases:

- Adding a valid item with a valid quantity
- Adding the same item twice (quantity should add up)
- Entering `abc`, `0` or `-2` as quantity
- Typing an item that isn't on the menu
- Removing an item that isn't in the cart
- Removing more than the quantity in the cart (item should get deleted)
- Typing `done` with an empty cart
- Checking the bill total by hand against the program's output

